From microsoft/onnxruntime-genai#2244 (merge commit f604a5ee6a226c9e8d8f1cfe992bb9a551d4d52c),
src/models/onnxruntime_inline.h only.

The fork pinned by OGA_REPO/OGA_REF resolves the OrtModelPackageApi entries
through Ort::Experimental::Get_*_SinceV28_Fn. ORT defines those accessors in
onnxruntime_experimental_cxx_api.h, which the fork does not include (it pulls in
onnxruntime_cxx_api.h, whose Ort:: types clash with the ones genai vendors). The
block is gated on ORT_API_VERSION >= 28, so it only compiles from ORT 1.28 on and
fails with C2653/C3861 against ORT 1.30. Upstream resolves the same functions
through OrtApi::GetExperimentalFunction and the C header's name constants.

Dropped: the PR's src/models/recurrent_state.{cpp,h} change. It makes
RecurrentState follow past_present_share_buffer on every EP, which is a
behavior change unrelated to the build break.

